# Every run artefact: plan.json, hints, the audit log, the minted identity file, the
# per-plan store. Regenerated by scripts/run_pipeline.py; none of it is anyone else's
# to read.
out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Downloaded source datasets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Fetched rather than vendored. They are 116 MB between them and their licences differ
# from this repository's:
#
#   data.gov.in "Train details"   -> Government Open Data Licence - India
#   Kaggle indian-railways        -> per that dataset's own terms
#
# scripts/import_opendata.py reads them and writes the extract below. Regenerate rather
# than passing them on.
data/Train_details_*.csv
data/IRCTC_cleaned.csv
data/schedules.json
data/schedules.json.zip
data/stations.json*
data/_imported.hold

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two files that are deliberately NOT ignored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# data/timetable_danapur.imported.csv
#
#   A 35 KB derived extract -- 543 services over one division, reduced to the ten columns
#   this model needs -- not a copy of any source book. Committing it is what makes a clone
#   plan against published times rather than the approximate ones, which is the difference
#   between demonstrating the idea and demonstrating the system. Its own header carries
#   the attribution and the regenerate-rather-than-copy note.
#
# web/public/plan.json
#
#   ~3.9 MB and rewritten on every pipeline run, so committing it adds a blob to history
#   each time. It stays tracked anyway: the client fetches /plan.json at runtime as a
#   static asset, and the build host has no Python or OR-Tools to regenerate it, so
#   ignoring it would leave a clean checkout deploying an app with no data in it. Repo
#   size is the cheaper problem. Regenerate and sync with:
#
#       python scripts/run_pipeline.py --days 7 --tasks 600 --monthly --validate
#       cd web && npm run sync
